## Stale doc comment references a page that no longer exists

### Status
Done.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
`ExternalLogin.cshtml.cs`'s XML doc comment on `OnPostConfirmationAsync` says the email-mismatch
path "sends a normal confirmation-email link and redirects to ConfirmEmailRequired," but the
actual code redirects to `./RegisterConfirmation` — `ConfirmEmailRequired` was consolidated away
as part of `BUGS-registration-confirmation-redirect.ospec` and doesn't exist in this repo.

### Motivation
A future contributor reading the doc comment to understand the redirect target, or grepping for
`ConfirmEmailRequired` while modifying this flow, gets pointed at a page that's gone — wasting
time or risking it being reintroduced as a duplicate of `RegisterConfirmation`, the exact
"two pages saying the same thing" problem the original consolidation was meant to eliminate.

### Proposed Changes
Update the doc comment on `OnPostConfirmationAsync` in `ExternalLogin.cshtml.cs` to say it
redirects to `RegisterConfirmation`, matching the actual code.

### Acceptance Criteria
- The doc comment no longer mentions `ConfirmEmailRequired`.

### Out of Scope
- No behavior change — comment wording only.

