## Dropped debug log line on wrong-password sign-in attempts

### Status
Done.

### GitHub Issue
None yet.

### Summary
`ApplicationSignInManager.CheckPasswordSignInAsync`'s wrong-password branch drops the base
`SignInManager`'s `Logger.LogDebug(EventIds.InvalidPassword, "User failed to provide the correct
password.")` call, and `Login.cshtml.cs` doesn't log anything on the generic `Failed` result
either — so this diagnostic signal is gone entirely, not just relocated.

### Motivation
An operator investigating a brute-force or credential-stuffing pattern against a specific account
by grepping logs for Identity's own "failed to provide the correct password" line will find
nothing from this app for wrong-password attempts, losing a signal the stock framework provides
by default.

### Proposed Changes
Reproduce the base `SignInManager`'s debug-log call in `ApplicationSignInManager`'s wrong-password
branch (`Logger.LogDebug(EventIds.InvalidPassword, ...)` or equivalent), so wrong-password
attempts are logged the same way they would be without this override.

### Acceptance Criteria
- A wrong-password sign-in attempt produces the same debug-level log entry the base
  `SignInManager` would produce, via `ApplicationSignInManager`.

### Out of Scope
- Any change to what `Login.cshtml.cs` itself logs on the generic `Failed` path.
